HY2 BBR uses the XTLS/Xray-core Go module at commit
d562d8947d3175db86b4fa849742433a9876cb63 (local reference: ref/Xray-core).
Only transport/internet/hysteria/congestion/bbr and congestion/common
are linked from that module, under MPL-2.0. The local adapter
internal/tunnel/hysteria_bbr.go is adapted from congestion/utils.go and
retains MPL-2.0: it narrows the connection interface, fixes the standard
profile, and omits Brutal/Reno selection. Both endpoints install BBR
after authentication. The QUIC implementation is github.com/apernet/quic-go
v0.61.1-0.20260806010916-184d081eef3e (MIT).
The mux selection follows mihomo's sing-mux integration. Veilink links
github.com/metacubex/sing-mux v0.3.10 and sing v0.5.8 (GPL-3.0-or-later),
with smux (MIT) and yamux (MPL-2.0); no mihomo implementation was copied.
